==Strategy==
Unless you have [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] units (e.g. [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] or [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] for {{4c}}), bring meatshields that can be killed fairly quickly by the other enemies so that Two Can misses his attacks. Note that the faster you clear the Gabriels/Brollows, the faster you'll have to face the Two Cans and Lemurrs. if you do use Octopus, it's a no-brainer to also bring Courier. He absolutely shreds Two Can while also being able to clear out the smaller enemies.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Tropical Kalisa (Uber Rare Cat)|Tropical Kalisa]] - Having 100 more standing range than Two Can, high DPS, and [[Massive Damage]] vs [[:Category:Red Enemies|Reds]], she can easily make short work of them (while also working well against the other enemies), she also has decent HP and rebound, so she can also effectively counter any wave Two Can makes with another attack. [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Sanada Yukimura]] works similarly, but needs more timing.
*[[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]] - Good range, DPS, and her piercing range means peons in the way won't stop her from hitting Two Can and LeMurr. Be wary though, as her high cost and blindspot can become her greater weaknesses here.
*[[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave Immune Ubers]] - They can work as a failsafe for when Octopus Cat fails to block a Two Can wave, making the battle easier.
*Any Uber with the Wave Shield ability can completely nullify the challenge of this stage. Examples include [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine MKIII]], [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Yamiinora]] and [[Hell Warden Emma (Uber Rare Cat)|Hell Commissioner Emma]].
*Ubers that aren't melee/tankers (With the exception of Cat Machine MKIII) can perform as backup attackers here as well.

